, 0.035993628203868866, 0.011148174293339252, 0.011381121352314949, -0.00048461282858625054, -0.014988470822572708, 0.017490986734628677, -0.019101647660136223, 0.010176452808082104, 0.01202006172388792, -0.012339531444013119, 0.017091648653149605, 0.031734026968479156, -0.014030060730874538, 0.0019151566084474325, 0.02322813682258129, 0.0016755539691075683, 0.003933475352823734, 0.002643947722390294, -0.00881204940378666, 0.009198076091706753, -0.04323495179414749, -0.02143111824989319, -0.004985064268112183, -0.005996719468384981, -0.0038602633867412806, -0.01106165163218975, 0.019926946610212326, -0.003817001823335886, 0.009277943521738052, 0.01811661571264267, 0.03988051414489746]], "input": ["# USDA and Nutritional Guidelines Community\n\nThe community is centered around the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) and its role in promoting public health through dietary guidelines. Key entities include the USDA, NUTRISOL, and food pyramids, which are interconnected through various relationships that emphasize nutritional analysis and dietary recommendations.\n\n## USDA's central role in public health nutrition\n\nThe USDA is a pivotal entity in this community, responsible for developing dietary guidelines that aim to improve public health. Its initiatives, such as the My Plate nutritional guide, are designed to educate the public on healthy eating habits. The USDA's comprehensive database of food composition and dietary surveys serves as a critical resource for understanding nutritional data, which is essential for both individuals and health professionals. The agency's influence extends to various organizations that reference its guidelines and data, highlighting its importance in shaping dietary practices across the nation. [Data: Entities (7853); Relationships (14153, 5951, 11634)]\n\n## NUTRISOL's utilization of USDA resources\n\nNUTRISOL, a program from the Department of Preventive Medicine at the University of Málaga, relies on the USDA's food composition database for its nutritional analysis. This relationship underscores the USDA's role as a foundational source of nutritional information that supports various health initiatives and research programs. By utilizing USDA data, NUTRISOL enhances its capability to conduct dietary surveys and analyses, thereby contributing to the broader understanding of nutrition and public health. [Data: Entities (8189); Relationships (16799)]\n\n## Food pyramids as educational tools\n\nThe food pyramids developed by the USDA serve as educational models that establish general dietary recommendations. These pyramids are integral to the USDA's efforts to promote healthy eating habits among the American population. By providing a visual representation of food groups and their recommended proportions, the food pyramids help individuals make informed dietary choices. This educational approach is crucial in addressing public health concerns related to nutrition and obesity. [Data: Entities (15373); Relationships (16800)]\n\n## Collaboration with other health organizations\n\nThe USDA collaborates with various health organizations, such as the American Heart Association and the World Health Organization (OMS), to provide comprehensive dietary guidelines. These collaborations enhance the credibility and reach of the USDA's recommendations, ensuring that they are aligned with global health standards. The partnerships also facilitate the sharing of nutritional data, which is vital for developing effective public health strategies. [Data: Relationships (11634, 5951)]\n\n## Impact of USDA guidelines on dietary practices\n\nThe dietary guidelines provided by the USDA have a significant impact on the eating habits of the American population. By promoting specific recommendations on cholesterol consumption and overall nutrition, the USDA plays a crucial role in shaping public awareness and behavior regarding healthy eating. The agency's initiatives, such as the My Plate guide, are designed to simplify nutritional information and make it accessible to families, thereby fostering healthier dietary choices. [Data: Entities (7853); Relationships (14153)]", "# GoCARB Project and Roche\n\nThe community centers around the GoCARB Project, an initiative by Roche aimed at improving dietary assessment methods. Roche is the primary organization behind this project, which is sponsored by the National Institutes of Health (NIH), indicating a significant collaboration in the field of dietary assessment technologies.\n\n## GoCARB Project's focus on dietary assessment\n\nThe GoCARB Project is a significant initiative aimed at enhancing dietary assessment methods. This project is crucial for improving how dietary data is collected and analyzed, which can lead to better health outcomes. The focus on dietary assessment is particularly relevant in today's context of rising health issues related to diet, making this project a key player in public health initiatives. [Data: Entities (8203), Relationships (16667)]\n\n## Roche's role in the GoCARB Project\n\nRoche is the organization behind the GoCARB Project, indicating its commitment to advancing dietary assessment technologies. As a major pharmaceutical company, Roche's involvement lends credibility and resources to the project, which could enhance its effectiveness and reach. The relationship between Roche and the GoCARB Project highlights the importance of corporate involvement in public health initiatives. [Data: Entities (8202), Relationships (17027)]\n\n## NIH sponsorship of the GoCARB Project\n\nThe National Institutes of Health (NIH) sponsors the GoCARB Project, which underscores the project's significance in the realm of dietary assessment technologies. NIH's involvement not only provides funding but also adds a layer of scientific rigor and validation to the project. This relationship is vital for ensuring that the project's outcomes are credible and can be effectively implemented in public health strategies. [Data: Relationships (16667)]\n\n## Collaboration between Roche and NIH\n\nThe collaboration between Roche and the NIH in the GoCARB Project exemplifies a strong partnership between the private and public sectors in addressing health-related issues. This partnership is essential for leveraging resources, expertise, and research capabilities to develop effective dietary assessment methods. Such collaborations can lead to innovative solutions that benefit public health on a larger scale. [Data: Relationships (16667, 17027)]", "# Global Food Security and Nutrition Community\n\nThis community is centered around key organizations and initiatives focused on global food security and nutrition, primarily led by the FAO, UNU, and various collaborating entities. The relationships among these organizations highlight their collaborative efforts to address pressing global challenges related to food safety, dietary guidelines, and nutrition education.\n\n## FAO's central role in global nutrition efforts\n\nThe Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) is a pivotal entity in this community, leading international efforts to combat hunger and enhance nutrition. Established as a specialized agency of the United Nations, the FAO provides essential dietary guidelines and international food composition tables that are crucial for understanding nutritional values. Its initiatives aim to improve nutrition and ensure food security worldwide, making it a cornerstone of global health efforts. The FAO's collaborations with various organizations, including the WHO and the European Union, further amplify its impact on food safety and nutrition standards [Data: Entities (875); Relationships (5193, 5198, 5156, 5195, 5202, +more)].\n\n## Collaboration with the World Health Organization\n\nThe FAO collaborates closely with the World Health Organization (WHO) to develop international guidelines and recommendations that address nutrition and food security. This partnership is vital for establishing global nutrition guidelines and food safety standards, ensuring that their efforts contribute to improved health and well-being worldwide. The joint initiatives between these organizations highlight the importance of a coordinated approach to tackling global health challenges related to nutrition [Data: Relationships (5198, 5195, 5202, +more)].\n\n## UNU's focus on research and capacity development\n\nThe United Nations University (UNU) plays a significant role in this community by focusing on research and capacity development related to global issues, including food security and nutrition. As an academic institution, UNU contributes to the understanding and resolution of pressing global challenges through its research initiatives. Its collaboration with the WHO on health-related research further emphasizes its commitment to addressing global health issues [Data: Entities (15308); Relationships (13943, 5202, +more)].\n\n## The role of the Comisión del Codex Alimentarius\n\nThe Comisión del Codex Alimentarius operates under the FAO to establish food safety standards globally. This body is crucial for standardizing food safety protocols, which are essential for ensuring that food systems are safe and effective. The Codex Alimentarius plays a vital role in protecting consumer health and ensuring fair practices in food trade, thereby contributing to global food security [Data: Entities (874); Relationships (5189, +more)].\n\n## Collaboration with the Sociedad Española de Nutrición Comunitaria\n\nThe Sociedad Española de Nutrición Comunitaria collaborates with the FAO to align dietary guidelines with international standards. This partnership is significant for promoting community nutrition in Spain and ensuring that local dietary practices are informed by global standards. The collaboration highlights the importance of integrating local and international efforts to improve nutrition and food security [Data: Entities (7893); Relationships (5197, +more)].", "# World Health Organization and Global Health Guidelines\n\nThe community is centered around the World Health Organization (WHO) and its relationships with various health-related entities, including guidelines on nutrition, alcohol consumption, and food safety. The WHO collaborates with organizations like the Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs and the International Carbohydrate Quality Consortium to promote health standards globally.\n\n## WHO's role in global health governance\n\nThe World Health Organization (WHO) is a pivotal entity in the realm of international public health, providing guidelines and recommendations that shape health policies worldwide. Its influence extends to various health topics, including nutrition, alcohol consumption, and disease management. The WHO's guidelines are critical for countries in formulating their health strategies, making it a cornerstone of global health governance. [Data: Entities (4684); Relationships (4103, 13942, 5198, 13938, 13941, +more)]\n\n## Impact of alcohol consumption on health\n\nAlcohol consumption is recognized as a significant lifestyle factor that can lead to various health issues, including osteoporosis. The WHO advises against excessive alcohol consumption due to its associated health risks, which include increased mortality and morbidity. This highlights the importance of public health campaigns aimed at reducing alcohol intake to improve overall health outcomes. [Data: Entities (7863); Relationships (11027, 11266, 13937, +more)]\n\n## Collaboration with the Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs\n\nThe Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs, Food Safety and Nutrition collaborates with the WHO to implement health guidelines in Spain. This partnership is crucial for ensuring that local health policies align with international standards, thereby enhancing public health initiatives and food safety measures within the country. [Data: Entities (7895); Relationships (13938)]\n\n## Nutritional guidelines and carbohydrate intake\n\nThe WHO provides essential recommendations regarding carbohydrate intake, which are vital for preventing health issues such as obesity and diabetes. The International Carbohydrate Quality Consortium works alongside the WHO to establish scientific consensus on carbohydrate quality, emphasizing the importance of these guidelines in promoting healthy dietary practices. [Data: Entities (7901); Relationships (7658, 13940)]\n\n## New classification of thyroid tumors\n\nThe WHO has made significant contributions to medical classifications, including the introduction of the Non-Invasive Follicular Thyroid Neoplasm with Papillary-like nuclear features (NIFTP) in its classification of thyroid tumors. This new category enhances the understanding of thyroid neoplasms and reflects the WHO's commitment to advancing medical knowledge and practices. [Data: Entities (4685); Relationships (13932, 13933)]", "# Nutrition in Older Adults Community\n\nThe community focuses on the study and promotion of nutrition specifically for older adults, featuring key contributors such as researchers and health organizations. The chapter titled 'Nutrición en el Adulto Mayor' serves as a central piece of work, with various entities contributing to its development and dissemination.\n\n## Centrality of 'Nutrición en el Adulto Mayor'\n\n'Nutrición en el Adulto Mayor' is a pivotal chapter that discusses nutrition for older adults, published in Madrid. This work serves as a foundational resource for understanding the nutritional needs of this demographic, highlighting the importance of tailored dietary guidelines. The chapter's publication in a major city like Madrid indicates its potential influence on health policies and practices in Spain and beyond. [Data: Entities (4811); Relationships (1314)]\n\n## Contributions from key researchers\n\nArtacho Martín Lagos, Ruiz López, and Quiles Morales are significant contributors to the chapter on nutrition for older adults. Their involvement underscores the collaborative nature of this research, which combines expertise from various fields to address the complex nutritional needs of older adults. Each researcher brings unique insights that enhance the chapter's credibility and relevance, making it a vital resource for practitioners and policymakers alike. [Data: Entities (4809, 4808, 4810); Relationships (14077, 14076, 14078)]\n\n## Role of the FAO in nutrition guidelines\n\nThe Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and information relevant to nutrition, including for older adults. Their involvement ensures that the chapter aligns with international standards and best practices, which can significantly impact public health initiatives. The FAO's global perspective on nutrition helps to contextualize the findings within broader health frameworks, making the chapter a valuable asset for global health discussions. [Data: Entities (4811); Relationships (5192)]\n\n## Support from the Spanish Ministry of Health\n\nThe Ministry of Health in Spain promotes health policies that include nutrition for older adults, indicating governmental support for the initiatives discussed in 'Nutrición en el Adulto Mayor.' This endorsement is critical for the implementation of effective nutrition programs and policies, as it highlights the importance of addressing the dietary needs of older adults at a national level. The ministry's involvement can facilitate funding and resources for further research and public health campaigns. [Data: Entities (4811); Relationships (5412)]", "# SENC and Global Nutrition Guidelines\n\nThe community is centered around the Sociedad Española de Nutrición Comunitaria (SENC) and its relationships with global health organizations like the World Health Organization (WHO). These entities collaborate to develop and promote nutritional guidelines aimed at improving public health, particularly for the general population and pediatric patients.\n\n## SENC's role in community nutrition\